<h2>Attributes of Rectangles, Rhombuses, and Squares</h2>
<h3>Warm-up: A–D original figures</h3><p>Source teacher confirms A,B,D have four sides (quadrilaterals) and C is triangle. Each original shape may be defended as odd one out for a true distinguishing property; check original visuals.</p>
<h3>Activity: Which belong?</h3><table class="source-chart"><thead><tr><th>Original source category</th><th>Defining properties</th><th>Student must do</th></tr></thead><tbody>
